AB  - The core of the current software delivery is the Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines, but the problem of reliability and efficient deployments under the rising system complexity, scale, and heterogeneity becomes highly challenging. Current CI/CD models mainly rely on reactive monitoring and fixed rule-based mechanisms which are not sufficient to predict failures and performance risks in new dynamic cloud-native settings. To address such shortcomings, this paper also suggests PA-ML-CI/CD, a predictive learningbased analytics solution that actively assesses the risk of deployment reliability and performance before the pipeline is executed. The framework incorporates multi-source CI/CD telemetry, feature engineering at scale, ensemble learning models and risk conscious deployment controller to make intelligent, preemptive deployment decisions. This research indicates the presence of the challenge in implementing predictive machine learning and risk-aware decision-making into CI/CD pipelines to support proactive, self-adaptive software delivery in large-scale cloud-native settings.
