AB  - Self-healing automation systems are a game-changer for dependable continuous integration, tackling the problem of test flakiness that affects current software creation. These smart systems use machine learning and adaptive fixes to spot, sort, and fix test failures on their own. By mixing LSTM networks for spotting patterns over time, gradient boosting for sorting, and reinforcement learning, these systems accurately tell apart real software problems from environmental issues. The design relies on microservices and event-driven setups, using Apache Kafka for streaming messages, Kubernetes for organization, and Prometheus for gathering metrics. This allows the system to handle millions of test events very quickly. Using anomaly detection strategies that combine statistical process control with deep learning, the system keeps different models for various test types and adapts constantly through online learning. The rollout happens in stages: watching, shadow mode, and gradual automation. This makes sure it fits smoothly with current CI/CD tools and boosts trust within the organization. These systems change quality assurance by cutting down on false positives, speeding up resolution times, and saving a lot of money through automatic fixes.
ER  - 

