AB  - Cloud computing has revolutionized application development by enabling scalable, flexible, and automated deployment. Kubernetes is at the heart of container orchestration and continuous integration. Although containerization and orchestration technologies are widely deployed, they have not yet been integrated into the High-Performance Computing (HPC) environment, especially for energy efficiency and smart workload distribution. The standard Kubernetes scheduling mechanisms tend to result in underutilized resources, and creating new custom schedulers introduces additional complexity, testing difficulty, and maintenance issues. This research presents an Energy-Efficient Container Orchestration (EE-CO) architecture for HPC workloads that combines Machine Learning (ML) with Kubernetes on the cloud infrastructure. EE-CO optimizes adaptive workload allocation, performance surveillance, and resource management in heterogeneous CPU architectures. It enhanced workload allocation efficiency and cost-effectiveness, and reduced energy consumption and computational costs. The potential of ML-powered Kubernetes orchestration for developing sustainable, scalable, and energy-efficient HPC deployments in the cloud.
