AB  - Security enforcement in Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines largely depends on static and rule-based analysis techniques, which are ineffective in identifying vulnerabilities that manifest during runtime execution. Exposure to security risks is worsened by the delay in the existing vulnerability discovery processes. Subsequently, this paper presents an AI-supported Runtime vulnerability prediction system which uses behavioral telemetry collected in CI/CD pipeline executions. The framework constantly guides the indicators of runtime, such as execution history, API communications and resource usage statistics, and uses a lightweight machine-learning model to predict the vulnerabilities at the earliest possible phases of the pipeline. The main contributions are: (i) introduction of runtime-aware security in CI/CD pipelines; (ii) development of telemetry-based behavioral features of vulnerability prediction and (iii) application of an efficient AI-based prediction model, which can be implemented in a real world environment. Experimental results prove that the vulnerability discovery capabilities can be better detected and have lower latency compared to traditional statical security tools. The suggested methodology, in its turn, strengthens proactive security in the DevSecOps ecosystems, which creates more resilient, secure development pipelines in the form of software delivery.
ER  - 

